So what supports your sky?  After spending a lot of time alone on the road, one cannot help but pull apart the bits and pieces of one's inner-workings.  Such is the nature of long distance travel, especially when it takes me over and through open, lonely country.  As I drive I turn my attention towards the sky, and I start to wonder what holds up my own internal sky.  For so long I had been propping it up with the idea of having to be at a certain place in life.  Where was this place?  It was a place near the end of the rainbow where I had a fulfilling job, a nice house, a wonderful mate, and a clear plan for the future.  I once had all those things[[
